    "body": "> Maybe this is related to the Shepherd definition scraper continuing to scrape non-exported parts of HTML despite us asking them not to?\r\n\r\nNo, it's completely unrelated. You can see with `bikeshed refs --type=dfn --text=environment --spec=html` that there are indeed 3, with 2 of them unexported.\r\n\r\nThe issue is that link-defaults causes matching dfns to be treated as exported for your spec's purposes (because you're explicitly asking for them!), the same as explicitly specifying the spec in an autolink. However, those three definitions are indistinguishable, so all three of them match the link-defaults entry and all get flipped on. They *should* all be fixed.\r\n\r\nThe first dfn @hober listed shouldn't be exposed as a definition to Bikeshed at all. You can specify this by giving it an empty linking text, with a `data-lt=\"\"` attribute. (All the dfns in this \"external dfns\" section should be doing this.)\r\n\r\nThe second dfn is missing its `for` value; there should be a `data-dfn-for=\"link processing options\"` on the `dl` to scope all the definitions there. All of these also probably *do* want to be exported, since other specs will need to reference them when defining their \"process a link header\" algos for their own link types.\r\n\r\nThe third is marked up correctly.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
