    "body": "> Our assumption is that since we did not add data-export=\"\" to these, it shouldn't matter how they are marked up.\r\n\r\nThat's not correct. They're still linkable definitions, keeping them unexported just makes them less immediately visible, to reduce accidental collisions. There are still ways for other specs to link to them, such as what happened in this thread. To actually tell Bikeshed that a definition *should not be picked up at all* (which is the case for every definition in this section, since none of them are being defined by HTML, but rather are using `dfn` for Wattsi-internal linking purposes), `data-lt=\"\"` is the correct markup.\r\n\r\n> HTML is the only spec which can define link types.\r\n\r\nOkay. It should still either be marked up appropriately in the Bikeshed data model so it can be distinguished from the other definition, or marked for Bikeshed to ignore it completely so nobody can reference it at all.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
