    "created_at": "2022-11-21T01:13:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-11-21T01:13:04Z",
    "body": "...yes? I have to be able to tell `dfn`s meant for Bikeshed to know about from ones that it shouldn't know about, and I can do so either by annotating every `dfn` that Bikeshed should know or by annotating every one it shouldn't know. The vast majority of specs want 100% of their definitions to be picked up by Bikeshed, and for the minority of exceptions, they still want the vast majority of their definitions to be. (HTML falls into this latter category - it has a small % of exceptions that it uses for its own tooling because Wattsi lacks the ability to autolink to external documents, but all the rest of its `dfn`s should be picked up.) So it makes much more sense for the rare spec to annotate its rare `dfn` when that case occurs.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure where this resistance is coming from. I can write the PR for you, if for some reason it's just a matter of not wanting to spend a few minutes on the task. If it's some more principled rejection of the entire idea, I'd love to understand your reasoning more.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
